==Ancient Greek==

===Alternative forms===
* {{grc-alt|κλέϝος|dial=pho}}

===Etymology===
From {{term|κλέϝος|tr=klewos|lang=grc|sc=polytonic}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|grc}} {{term/t|ine-pro|*ḱléwos}}.  Cognates include Sanskrit {{term|श्रवस्|tr=śrávas|lang=sa|sc=Deva}}, Avestan {{term|𐬵𐬀𐬬𐬀𐬭𐬯|tr=sravah|lang=ae}}, Old Armenian {{term|լու||sc=Armn|tr=lu|lang=xcl}}, {{term|լսեմ||sc=Armn|tr=lsem|lang=xcl}}, Old Church Slavonic {{term|слово|tr=slovo|lang=cu|sc=Cyrs}}, and Old Irish {{term|clú|lang=sga}}.  Compare {{term|κλύω||I hear|tr=kluō|lang=grc|sc=polytonic}} and {{term|κλέω|lang=grc}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{grc-ipa-rows|k|l|e'|.|o|s}}

===Noun===
{{grc-noun|κλέους|n|third|kleos}}

# [[rumour]], [[report]]
# good report, [[fame]], [[glory]]
# {{context|rare|lang=grc}} bad report, [[disrepute]]

